Package: bayesSampleMix
Type: Package
Title: Contamination-Aware Bayesian Integration of Probability and
    Non-Probability Samples
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Diego Andres", "Perez Ruiz", email = "diego.perezruiz@manchester.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")),
    person("Constanza", "Avalos Valdebenito", email = "constanza.avalos@postgrad.manchester.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cph"))
  )
Description: Bayesian contamination-mixture regression for combining a
    trusted probability sample with a non-probability sample that may
    contain units incompatible with the target model. Each non-probability
    unit carries a latent compatibility indicator that is sampled by data
    augmentation, yielding posterior inference for regression coefficients,
    the contamination fraction and unit-level filter scores. Gaussian
    (conjugate Gibbs), logistic (Polya-Gamma augmentation; Polson, Scott and
    Windle (2013) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2013.829001>) and Poisson
    (Laplace-proposal Metropolis-Hastings) regressions are supported, with an
    optional Mahalanobis-type covariate term that flags units outside the
    covariate support of the probability sample.
